{"id": "c8a6f0af-d700-4a79-bced-0b875dbcf75d", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "With only 2 invocations in 24 hours, both were likely cold starts, and the overhead latency numbers confirm minimal real traffic. Given that, provisioned concurrency would be billed continuously regardless of use, making it a poor trade-off unless there's a strict latency SLO—better to consider smaller containers or other alternatives.

A cheaper option is a scheduled keep-warm ping via EventBridge, though that's unofficial and only keeps one instance warm; also worth noting MaxConcurrency is 1, so provisioned concurrency can't exceed that. I should flag that I haven't verified current pricing and should point to the pricing page instead. The sample itself is quite small since the endpoint was only created about 30 minutes ago, so the invocation history is naturally thin.

"}]}
